      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: to clarify, it is quieter with -80. However, the docs state that -80 should be silent; it is in fact not quite silent, but close.\n\nEdit: To be clear, the expected behavior is that an avatar gain limit of -80 should _completely_ silence all avatar audio sources; the actual behavior is that it makes them very quiet, but not entirely silent. It's possible that this is just a doc bug; I expect that setting far=0 might work as an alternative way of silencing avatars.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
